  "limitations": [
    "Single sequential pair at each of two sizes, not replicated full60 crossover trials. Full15 opposite order supports direction but does not establish statistical significance.",
    "Mixed preparation accounts for about 71.7% of the 4194.831669s CPU difference; shared coverage annotation differs by 456.228s and loading by 880.271s. The full delta is not attributable to SQL.",
    "Hybrid-first full60 left file cache in the shared allocation. Native late annotation hit the 192GiB cgroup limit with 172 max events, zero OOM and zero swap. Both worker process peaks were reached by input60 before these events.",
    "No per-arm minimum safe allocation, I/O-byte saving, fully out-of-core bound, cross-configuration result or whole-pipeline saving is established.",
    "The single ordinary consumer and its outputs pass exact scientific proof under existing comparison rules. This is compatibility evidence only, with no matched output performance pair; unchanged mitochondrial inputs do not prove hybrid mitochondrial burden behavior.",
    "No GC changes were added after freezing. Results do not predict a subsequently modified hybrid."
  ],
